  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper evaluates a hybrid Quantum Transfer Learning (QTL) model combining a frozen 3‑layer classical MLP feature extractor with a 4‑qubit variational quantum circuit on a 32,580‑instance credit risk dataset. The hybrid model achieves 91.08% accuracy and AUC 0.8797, slightly exceeding a classical neural network baseline (90.90% accuracy, AUC 0.8477) and substantially outperforming a standalone QNN (80.97% accuracy, AUC 0.7446), especially in minority-class recall (0.62 vs 0.16). All experiments are conducted on a simulator using PennyLane.",
